<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    HSK patch: gate VFE Pirates Junker raids by adding a
    raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve so they don't appear in early-game /
    low-wealth / tribal scenarios.

    Why?
    Junker faction is industrial-tier (warcasket pirates with guns and
    SMGs), but its weakest pawn — VFEP_Scrapper — has combatPower 65.
    That means at ~25k wealth on day 4 of a Neolithic Norbal start,
    the storyteller's raid budget (~200-400 points) is enough to fit
    3-5 scrappers and the Junker faction qualifies as a raid source.
    Result: tribal stone-age colony gets raided by industrial pirates
    with shotguns and SMGs.

    Note: previous attempt used <minTotalPoints> on each pawnGroupMaker.
    That field doesn't exist on PawnGroupMaker — RimWorld silently
    ignored it (XML errors in log) and the patch was a no-op. The
    correct mechanism is raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve on the
    FactionDef itself: when commonality reaches 0, the storyteller
    can't pick the faction for a raid.

    The Junker FactionDef in VFE Pirates has NO raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve
    by default (the factions in Factions_Misc.xml inherit FactionBase
    which doesn't define one), so this patch ADDS the field.

    Curve:
        (0, 0)        — no raids at any low budget
        (799, 0)      — still 0 right up to the threshold
        (800, 0.001)  — barely above 0 at the threshold (sharp step)
        (1500, 1)     — full normal weight at mid-game
        (3000, 1.5)   — slightly higher weight at late game

    The (799, 0) → (800, 0.001) step is intentional — it produces an
    effectively step-function gate while keeping the curve interpolated
    (RimWorld curves require monotonic-x).
-->
<Patch>

    <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="VFEP_Junkers"]</xpath>
        <value>
            <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
                <points>
                    <li>(0, 0)</li>
                    <li>(799, 0)</li>
                    <li>(800, 0.001)</li>
                    <li>(1500, 1)</li>
                    <li>(3000, 1.5)</li>
                </points>
            </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
        </value>
    </Operation>

</Patch>
